f-3b1d-56b6-83df-ab24221da7ee'}, {'abstract': 'In a last-ditch effort to fulfill her promise of delivering Brexit, Britain’s prime minister dangled a final sacrifice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/podcasts/the-daily/brexit-uk-theresa-may.html', 'snippet': 'In a last-ditch effort to fulfill her promise of delivering Brexit, Britain’s prime minister dangled a final sacrifice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listen and subscribe to our podcast from your mobile device: Via Apple Podcasts | Via RadioPublic | Via Stitcher', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Agony of Being Theresa May', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Theresa M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Great Britain Withdrawal from EU (Brexit)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'subsection_name': 'The Daily', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aba9020-e0b3-5e60-80ea-752ed156651e', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aba9020-e0b3-5e60-80ea-752ed156651e'}, {'abstract': 'Across the world, economists have had to downgrade growth forecasts. It’s not as bad as it sounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/opinion/economy-debt-inflation.html', 'snippet': 'Across the world, economists have had to downgrade growth forecasts. It’s not as bad as it sounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year looked like the time when President Trump had delivered on his promises to strengthen the economy. His tax cuts appeared to juice growth above 3 percent, a pace the United States had not topped since 2005. But on Thursday the Commerce Department revised 2018 growth downward to below 3 percent, even as forecasts for 2019 were also trending lower, toward 2 percent. It all has triggered another wave of disappointed commentary about doggedly “slow” growth in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01sharmaWeb/merlin_152640414_ac7914ce-13a3-46f1-9782-58a27dc6d32f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01sharmaWeb/merlin_152640414_ac7914ce-13a3-46f1-9782-58a27dc6d32f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01sharmaWeb/merlin_152640414_ac7914ce-13a3-46f1-9782-58a27dc6d32f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01sharmaWeb/merlin_152640414_ac7914ce-13a3-46f1-9782-58a27dc6d32f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01sharmaWeb/01sharmaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01sharmaWeb/01sharmaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01sharmaWeb/01sharmaWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Miracle Years Are Over. Get Used to It.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruchir Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruchir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b238c4da-020d-5473-ba67-8f4abb7d1d64', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b238c4da-020d-5473-ba67-8f4abb7d1d64'}, {'abstract': 'At new museums, the past is finally becoming more than the story of men and wars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/opinion/tennessee-state-museum-quilts.html', 'snippet': 'At new museums, the past is finally becoming more than the story of men and wars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — Like many girls of my generation in the rural South, I learned every form of handwork my grandmother or great-grandmother could teach me: sewing, knitting, crocheting, quilting. I even learned to tat, a kind of handwork done with a tiny shuttle that turns thread into lace. Some of my happiest memories are of sitting on the edge of my great-grandmother’s bed, our heads bent together over a difficult project, as she pulled out my mangled stitches and patiently demonstrated the proper way to do them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01renkl2/merlin_152781546_c7b22b97-ac3e-40a0-b8d0-6d87a92e4dff-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01renkl2/merlin_152781546_c7b22b97-ac3e-40a0-b8d0-6d87a92e4dff-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01renkl2/merlin_152781546_c7b22b97-ac3e-40a0-b8d0-6d87a92e4dff-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01renkl2/merlin_152781546_c7b22b97-ac3e-40a0-b8d0-6d87a92e4dff-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01renkl2/01renkl2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01renkl2/01renkl2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01renkl2/01renkl2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waking Up to History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quilts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History (Academic Subject)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Renkl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Renkl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ce4096-df1b-5812-8fc5-7bb2c19aaed6', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ce4096-df1b-5812-8fc5-7bb2c19aaed6'}, {'abstract': 'Someday, Trump will not be in office. Congress needs a full accounting of his misdeeds to ensure they don’t happen again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/opinion/mueller-report-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Someday, Trump will not be in office. Congress needs a full accounting of his misdeeds to ensure they don’t happen again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Sunday, Attorney General William Barr sent us a letter summarizing what he says are the “principal conclusions” of the special counsel, Robert Mueller. The next day, together with five other committee chairmen, I wrote back to the attorney general, demanding that he provide us with the full Mueller report — not a summary, but the full report and all of the relevant evidence — by April 2.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01nadlerWeb/merlin_152608410_ae1f189b-1dc9-42c5-9750-2ebe2a160ba6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01nadlerWeb/merlin_152608410_ae1f189b-1dc9-42c5-9750-2ebe2a160ba6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01nadlerWeb/merlin_152608410_ae1f189b-1dc9-42c5-9750-2ebe2a160ba6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01nadlerWeb/merlin_152608410_ae1f189b-1dc9-42c5-9750-2ebe2a160ba6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01nadlerWeb/01nadlerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01nadlerWeb/01nadlerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01nadlerWeb/01nadlerWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America Is Done Waiting for the Mueller Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We’re Done Waiting for Mueller’s Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Prosecutors (Independent Counsel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, William P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerrold L. Nadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerrold', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Nadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2154d391-c373-572a-a1bf-7151c7953614', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2154d391-c373-572a-a1bf-7151c7953614'}, {'abstract': 'The attempt to exclude trans women from the ranks of women reinforces the dangerous idea that there is a right way to be female.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/opinion/trans-women-feminism.html', 'snippet': 'The attempt to exclude trans women from the ranks of women reinforces the dangerous idea that there is a right way to be female.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who counts as a woman? Is there some set of core experiences distinctive of womanhood, some shared set of adventures and exploits that every woman will encounter on her journey from diapers to the grave? The recent debates over the experiences of trans women gives us new reason to return to a question feminists have been grappling with for decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01stoneNew/01stoneNew-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/01/opinion/01stoneNew/01stoneNew-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo',