ilures and Blackouts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T15:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Virginia López Glass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Virginia', 'middlename': 'López', 'lastname': 'Glass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d37171d-1719-5517-8eea-73ec6074c1d5', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d37171d-1719-5517-8eea-73ec6074c1d5'}, {'abstract': 'A look at one of the words from last week’s puzzles that stumped our solvers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/crosswords/what-the-heck-is-that-crosswords-pips.html', 'snippet': 'A look at one of the words from last week’s puzzles that stumped our solvers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, this week’s “What the Heck Is That?” could be all about the singers who accompanied the soul singer Gladys Knight in hits such as “Midnight Train to Georgia,” because heaven knows that without them, she would have been known simply as “Gladys Knight and the.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/crosswords/01wordplay-heck-art-pips/01wordplay-heck-art-pips-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/01/crosswords/01wordplay-heck-art-pips/01wordplay-heck-art-pips-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/crosswords/01wordplay-heck-art-pips/01wordplay