ditionally, gravlax is salmon cured with salt and spices. Tracklements adds smoking to the process, resulting in salmon that’s mild (though rich), with a hint of smoke. Another new smoked salmon on the roster is cured with ras-el-hanout, the Moroccan spice blend, for a stronger flavor, with a whiff of cumin and pepper. The salmon, sold in one piece, is easy to slice.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner5/01burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner5/01burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner5/01burner5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner5/01burner5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner5/01burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner5/01burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner5/01burner5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gravlax With a Twist', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Slice: Gravlax With a Hint Of Woodsy Flavor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Durham's Tracklements and Smokery", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANN ARBOR (MICH)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T23:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40fc5649-dadb-57a6-93cf-1e548aa7a356', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40fc5649-dadb-57a6-93cf-1e548aa7a356'}, {'abstract': 'At Charlie Bird restaurant in SoHo, the public is invited to join the staff as the wine director introduces three wines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/dining/drinks/wine-lesson-charlie-bird.html', 'snippet': 'At Charlie Bird restaurant in SoHo, the public is invited to join the staff as the wine director introduces three wines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are wine classes galore in New York, but Charlie Bird restaurant in SoHo offers an insider’s approach: The tastings, intended for staff, are open to the public free of charge, once a week with a reservation. Grant Reynolds, the wine director and a partner, runs the lively program. Three wines are usually sampled and explained, he said, and all can be found at his Parcelle Wine.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner7/merlin_152686011_2a3f6d7a-e7ae-4a67-b27f-f7b7f5ad0e60-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner7/merlin_152686011_2a3f6d7a-e7ae-4a67-b27f-f7b7f5ad0e60-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner7/merlin_152686011_2a3f6d7a-e7ae-4a67-b27f-f7b7f5ad0e60-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner7/merlin_152686011_2a3f6d7a-e7ae-4a67-b27f-f7b7f5ad0e60-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner7/03burner7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner7/03burner7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner7/03burner7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Attend the Staff Wine Lesson', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Appreciate: Public Invited to Attend Staff Wine Lesson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Bird (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T23:04:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a00c423a-d513-521b-b39b-2295df7adf83', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a00c423a-d513-521b-b39b-2295df7adf83'}, {'abstract': 'Cédric Grolet, the pastry chef at Le Meurice in Paris, will spend a long weekend at Dominique Ansel Bakery serving his confections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/dining/cedric-grolet-pastry-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'Cédric Grolet, the pastry chef at Le Meurice in Paris, will spend a long weekend at Dominique Ansel Bakery serving his confections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cédric Grolet — the award-winning pastry chef at Le Meurice, one of Paris’s grand hotels — will take up residence at Dominique Ansel’s bakery in SoHo from Friday through Sunday. He will work with Mr. Ansel and his staff to make some of his dazzling confections mimicking fruits and nuts — lemons, strawberries and hazelnuts, with various fillings — each an individual serving about the size of a lemon. They will be sold each day until supplies run out.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/dining/01burner2/01burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 861, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/01/dining/01burner2/01burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 861}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/dining/01burner2/01burner2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 714, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/dining/01burner2/01burner2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1427, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/dining/01burner2/01burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/01/dining/01burner2/01burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/01/dining/01burner2/01burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parisian Pastry Pop-Up', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Marvel: Star Parisian Pastry Chef Pops Up in SoHo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pastries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grolet, Cedric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-01T23:05:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a636375-9880-55d1-9667-36d2836a762e', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a636375-9880-55d1-9667-36d2836a762e'}, {'abstract': '“Fromages,” a new book by the cheesemaker Dominique Bouchait, looks at French cheeses and how they’re made.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/01/dining/fromages-book-dominique-bouchait.html', 'snippet': '“Fromages,” a new book by the cheesemaker Dominique Bouchait, looks at French cheeses and how they’re made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his informative book, “Fromages,” Dominique Bouchait explains French cheeses, dividing them into “families,” according to how they’re made, like cooked and uncooked or blue-veined. But what he says about the French varieties applies to cheeses from anywhere. Though Mr. Bouchait — a master cheesemaker based in southwest France — focuses on the 45 French cheeses that have government-controlled names, his broad scope includes types of milk, raw and pasteurized cheeses, ripening, storage, fat content, wine pairings (he prefers white) and 40 recipes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner1/03burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 256, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner1/03burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 256}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner1/03burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner1/03burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/dining/03burner1/03burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda