erson': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/496114d5-5573-5cf2-81c0-eebcf7b88598', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/496114d5-5573-5cf2-81c0-eebcf7b88598'}, {'abstract': 'The findings of a test well drilled in Alaska three decades ago have been a closely guarded secret. We found answers in a Cleveland courthouse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/02/us/arctic-oil-drilling-well-data.html', 'snippet': 'The findings of a test well drilled in Alaska three decades ago have been a closely guarded secret. We found answers in a Cleveland courthouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANCHORAGE — Working through two winters in the biting arctic cold, roustabouts bored three miles deep into the coastal plain of northeast Alaska in search of oil. In the spring of 1986, they packed up and left, uttering not a word about what they had found and leaving only a short section of steel pipe to mark the spot.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/29/obituaries/archives/00articwell-KIC2/fileupload-1553875217725-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/03/29/obituaries/archives/00articwell-KIC2/fileupload-1553875217725-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/29/obituaries/archives/00articwell-KIC2/fileupload-1553875217725-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/29/obituaries/archives/00articwell-KIC2/fileupload-1553875217725-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1412, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/29/obituaries/archives/00articwell-KIC2/00articwell-KIC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/03/29/obituaries/archives/00articwell-KIC2/00articwell-KIC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/29/obituaries/archives/00articwell-KIC2/00articwell-KIC2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Key to the Arctic’s Oil Riches Lies Hidden in Ohio', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arctic Oil Well Hid Its Secrets For 3 Decades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC NATIONAL WILDLIFE REFUGE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reserves (Natural Resources)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Oil Co', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-02T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Investigative', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Eder and Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d230f24-f4da-5607-a40c-08607ce32638', 'word_count': 2241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d230f24-f4da-5607-a40c-08607ce32638'}, {'abstract': 'His wild, profane creations confront us with everything horrifying and joyous about America — and ourselves. Now he’s coming for Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/02/magazine/taylor-mac-gary-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'His wild, profane creations confront us with everything horrifying and joyous about America — and ourselves. Now he’s coming for Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine that you’re sitting in a theater, that you’ve been sitting there for 19 hours, with five more to go. Well, not only sitting. At times, you’ve been asked by the show’s maestro and star, the drag queen and performance artist Taylor Mac, to dash across the room to re-enact the Oklahoma Land Rush, or in a ritualized recompense for white flight, to “move to the suburbs” by surrendering your coveted orchestra seat to someone who was stuck in the back. You’ve grown used to the surprises of this piece, a 24-hour-long concert in which Mac works his way through 246 songs that were popular in America from 1776 to the present, interspersed with a radical narrative of American history. You came expecting that you would be challenged, provoked, entertained — why else sign up for a full-day, participatory history lesson administered by a queen who is currently wearing a macramé owl with a yellow-brick tail (a homage to Judy Garland and the Stonewall riots), a sequined miniskirt, a camouflage cape with cutout psychedelic peace signs and an iridescent Afro/space helmet? — but you aren’t prepared for what comes next.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-Mac-image5/07mag-Mac-image5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-Mac-image5/07mag-Mac-image5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-Mac-image5/07mag-Mac-image5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-Mac-image5/07mag-Mac-image5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-Mac-image5/07mag-Mac-image5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-Mac-image5/07mag-Mac-image5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-Mac-image5/07mag-