n outsider in a city that has often picked insiders. She is also Chicago’s first openly gay mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/02/us/chicago-election-results.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Lightfoot, a former federal prosecutor, ran as an outsider in a city that has often picked insiders. She is also Chicago’s first openly gay mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Chicago became the largest American city ever to elect a black woman as its mayor as voters on Tuesday chose Lori Lightfoot, a former prosecutor, to replace Rahm Emanuel. When she takes office in May, Ms. Lightfoot also will be the city’s first openly gay mayor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lori Lightfoot Is Elected Chicago Mayor, Becoming First Black Woman to Lead City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chicago Elects a Mayor Unlike Its First 55: A Gay Black Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lightfoot, Lori', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preckwinkle, Toni', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-02T22:56:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman, Mitch Smith and Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'las