ve Polastri (Sandra Oh). And although the source materials for “Killing Eve” are nominally Luke Jennings’s slick novellas, the show was built on a jumble of pop culture inputs. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wild Inspirations for ‘Killing Eve’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inspirations  For ‘Killing Eve’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Killing Eve (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kenzo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waller-Bridge, Phoebe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comer, Jodie (1993- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Favorite Murder (Radio Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'No Country for Old Men (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qualley, Margaret', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simpson, Angela (1975- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-03T07:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b6b33f2-00ac-5f0e-ae3d-a8931bbb23fe', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b6b33f2-00ac-5f0e-ae3d-a8931bbb23fe'}, {'abstract': 'When winter finally comes to the HBO epic with one last batch of episodes, it has a lot to answer for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/03/arts/television/game-of-thrones-season-8-questions.html', 'snippet': 'When winter finally comes to the HBO epic with one last batch of episodes, it has a lot to answer for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Season 7 finale of “Game of Thrones,” Jon Snow and Daenerys Targaryen hooked up, Viserion demolished the Wall, Arya killed Littlefinger and Jaime finally left Cersei. By the end the show had boiled the roughly 9,000 subplots it introduced over seven seasons down to two: Jon and Dany’s coalition of the willing vs. Cersei and Euron the mad pirate. And the White Walkers vs. everyone.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/arts/07got-plot-1/07got-plot-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/07/arts/07got-plot-1/07got-plot-1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/arts/07got-plot-1/07got-plot-1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/arts/07got-plot-1/07got-plot-1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/arts/07got-plot-1/07got-plot-1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/07/arts/07got-plot-1/07got-plot-1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 's