organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ea87db3-cea4-52d7-af2c-00f65ab56f88', 'word_count': 1570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ea87db3-cea4-52d7-af2c-00f65ab56f88'}, {'abstract': 'The story of one activist is the story of Egypt: What went wrong after the 2011 revolution?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/03/opinion/egypt-activist-alaa-abd-el-fattah-prison-release.html', 'snippet': 'The story of one activist is the story of Egypt: What went wrong after the 2011 revolution?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — We woke to the news last Friday: The 37-year-old software-developer and pro-democracy activist Alaa Abd El Fattah had finally been released from prison, after completing a five-year sentence for having called for street protests in defiance of the law. “Alaa is out. Yes, I swear,” tweeted his sister, Mona Seif, in Arabic. Not long after, she shared a blurry photo of him, sitting on a rattan chair at their family home, playing with their dog. Next came a photo of Alaa sitting with his now seven-year-old-son and holding the boy’s little feet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/opinion/03elrashidi/merlin_136650012_d7b95857-cf7c-4641-9032-f55ea77229a2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/03/opinion/03elrashidi/merlin_136650012_d7b95857-cf7c-4641-9032-f55ea77229a2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/opinion/03elrashidi/merlin_136650012_d7b95857-cf7c-4641-9032-f55ea77229a2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '