None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b74159b-9dd1-5c46-a5ad-57eb854c6940', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b74159b-9dd1-5c46-a5ad-57eb854c6940'}, {'abstract': 'A bittersweet song for our tortured world, dispensing light and dark equally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/04/magazine/poem-sometimes-there-is-a-day.html', 'snippet': 'A bittersweet song for our tortured world, dispensing light and dark equally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nimble lyrics of the Palestinian-American poet Naomi Shihab Nye can feel like manna descending. When the path seems bleakest, her words part gloom’s veil for one wondrous instant so that we can go on, even though the sorrow remains undiminished. Composed in cadences reminiscent of fables, this poem is a bittersweet song for our tortured world, dispensing light and dark equally as it imparts — with a candor usually reserved for children or griots — yet another chapter in the eternally calamitous tale of humanity. Selected by Rita Dove', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-07poem-t_CA0/07mag-07poem-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 99, 'width': 360, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/magazine/07mag-07poem-t_CA0/07mag-07poem-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 99, 'width': 360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Sometimes There Is a Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-04T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naomi Shihab Nye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Shihab', 'lastname': 'Nye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed9a2ef8-539e-54bd-b2a6-463e478f704a', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed9a2ef8-539e-54bd-b2a6-463e478f704a'}, {'abstract': 'A South Carolina college student was killed last weekend by a man posing as a ride-share driver, the police said. Across the country, women have reported dozens of similar attacks in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/04/us/fake-uber-driver-assaults.html', 'snippet': 'A South Carolina college student was killed last weekend by a man posing as a ride-share driver, the police said. Across the country, women have reported dozens of similar attacks in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The black sedan glided up to the Las Vegas hotel where Elizabeth Suarez was waiting to take an Uber home after a night of gambling. She recalled asking the driver: Are you waiting for Liz? Yeah, he responded. Get in.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/us/04fakeuber-01-promo/merlin_153021360_1978b7d4-2e47-4c8e-b548-36a7b7b27130-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/04/us/04fakeuber-01-promo/merlin_153021360_1978b7d4-2e47-4c8e-b548-36a7b7b27130-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/us/04fakeuber-01-promo/merlin_153021360_1978b7d4-2e47-4c8e-b548-36a7b7b27130-jumbo.jpg', 'height':