laine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35898f69-6d17-558d-b315-acbe7dc8e413', 'word_count': 1757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35898f69-6d17-558d-b315-acbe7dc8e413'}, {'abstract': 'For Democrats, an intense effort to rebuild their Midwestern “blue wall” for 2020 is showing gains in Michigan and Pennsylvania. But Wisconsin looks up for grabs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/04/us/politics/wisconsin-2020.html', 'snippet': 'For Democrats, an intense effort to rebuild their Midwestern “blue wall” for 2020 is showing gains in Michigan and Pennsylvania. But Wisconsin looks up for grabs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — With their recent selection of Milwaukee for their party’s 2020 convention, Democrats left little doubt that they believe their path to the White House runs through the Midwest in general and Wisconsin in particular.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/us/politics/04wisco2020-1/merlin_151930650_b7672241-19c0-44b5-bf56-af5b1fd58baf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/04/us/politics/04wisco2020-1/merlin_151930650_b7672241-19c0-44b5-bf56-af5b1fd58baf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/us/politics/04wisco2020-1/merlin_151930650_b7672241-19c0-44b5-bf56-af5b1fd58baf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/us/politics/04wisco2020-