r Thursday Evening Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Evening Briefing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-04-04T22:16:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Remy Tumin and Marcus Payadue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Remy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tumin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Payadue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/169d7b8c-d3a0-5484-9e3c-2cbb856ea0dc', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/169d7b8c-d3a0-5484-9e3c-2cbb856ea0dc'}, {'abstract': 'After participated in controversial studies by Timothy Leary involving hallucinogens, he continued researching alternate states of consciousness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/04/obituaries/ralph-metzner-dead.html', 'snippet': 'After participated in controversial studies by Timothy Leary involving hallucinogens, he continued researching alternate states of consciousness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ralph Metzner, a psychotherapist who began his career working with Timothy Leary on controversial studies at Harvard involving LSD and other drugs, then spent a lifetime exploring and writing about expanded consciousness in all sorts of cultures and settings, died on March 14 at his home in Sonoma, Calif. He was 82.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/obituaries/08Metzner1/merlin_152965509_351e93d6-0ea9-4572-bf0f-c17f00455730-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'im