dc2-b4e6e9fb46d3', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d69f4d9-d068-52b8-adc2-b4e6e9fb46d3'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s “Star Trek: Discovery,” we travel to Boreth, a sacred Klingon planet, where Pike finds out about his future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/04/arts/television/star-trek-discovery-through-the-valley-of-shadows-recap.html', 'snippet': 'In this week’s “Star Trek: Discovery,” we travel to Boreth, a sacred Klingon planet, where Pike finds out about his future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most problematic episodes of “Star Trek: Discovery” have involved Klingons, and “Through the Valley of Shadows” continues that trend of writers on the show having difficulty getting themselves out of self-created holes from past episodes. But I’ll say this: The scenes on Boreth, the sacred Klingon planet, gave a depth to Klingons rarely seen in the Trek franchise. Instead of lusting for battle and honor, we see a thoughtful, contemplative version of the race. (We’ve spent time on Boreth before, in a “Next Generation” episode called “Rightful Heir.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/arts/television/04trekrecap/04trekrecap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/04/arts/television/04trekrecap/04trekrecap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/arts/television/04trekrecap/04trekrecap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/04/arts/television/04trekrecap/04trekrecap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_n