ype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU/03tmag-petite-h-slide-B8BU-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Make T Something | Godefroy de Virieu', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Handicrafts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-05T17:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gautier Billotte', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gautier', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Billotte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c3315909-0dac-51ba-98d6-2cdbc8367c43', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c3315909-0dac-51ba-98d6-2cdbc8367c43'}, {'abstract': 'The creative director of Hermès’s Petit H atelier, Godefroy de Virieu, puts his imaginative approach to materials to new use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/05/t-magazine/make-a-shirt-from-new-york-times.html', 'snippet': 'The creative director of Hermès’s Petit H atelier, Godefroy de Virieu, puts his imaginative approach to materials to new use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The guiding principle at Petit H, the innovative atelier that transforms discarded materials from the workshops of Hermès into one-of-a-kind objects, is to work with what you have. For Godefroy de Virieu, the studio’s creative director, the most readily available materials are usually scraps of printed silk twill and calfskin leather — two hallmarks of the French luxury house — which he and his team refashion into everything from multicolor shoelaces to eye masks to animal-shaped shoe brushes. Given this knack for crafting treasures from unlikely components, we invited de Virieu to take part in our Make T Something series, for which a person must create something in under one hour using only basic crafting supplies, a copy of The New York Times and one wild-card item of their choosing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ/03tmag-petite-h-slide-BYBJ-superJum