': 'If you can paste it to a poster board, you can be it. Probably.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Calling all dreamers, all procrastinators, all people who’ve aged out of wunderkind status (happy 27th birthday, by the way): Stop doing nothing to make your hopes come true and start a vision board! A vision board is a collection of inspiring images, quotes and objects that turns your most important goals into accomplishments. Sound too good to be true? Before I made a vision board, I was like you — skeptical, sad and wearing jeans that didn’t work for my body type. But, now here I am, giving advice on how to be happy!', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07loose/07loose-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07loose/07loose-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07loose/07loose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07loose/07loose-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1457, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07loose/07loose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07loose/07loose-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07loose/07loose-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make a Vision Board That Works, for Real This Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vision Board That Really Works', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-06T18:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Kraut', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kraut', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa8389e4-bda1-5a80-a439-a1d7b63c244d', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa8389e4-bda1-5a80-a439-a1d7b63c244d'}, {'abstract': 'The language portraying second jobs as liberating or glamorous masks the reality of the insecure working lives of many Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/06/opinion/sunday/tax-day-side-hustle.html', 'snippet': 'The language portraying second jobs as liberating or glamorous masks the reality of the insecure working lives of many Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An attractive woman behind the wheel of a gray car says to the camera, “These days anyone can have a side hustle.” She then whisks off to the gym, for her other job as a personal trainer, beaming as she goes from one gig to another. This ad for the ride-share company Uber seeks to entice new drivers to join their ranks by using the “side hustle” come-on. The company isn’t alone. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07quart/merlin_142164918_d948d8b3-c61a-47a7-8d77-0309297a76aa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07quart/merlin_142164918_d948d8b3-c61a-47a7-8d77-0309297a76aa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07quart/merlin_142164918_d948d8b3-c61a-47a7-8d77-0309297a76aa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07quart/merlin_142164918_d948d8b3-c61a-47a7-8d77-0309297a76aa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07quart/07quart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07quart/07quart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07quart/07quart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Con of the Side Hustle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Con of the Side Hustle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freelancing, Self-Employment and Independent Contracting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-06T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa Quart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/26f3ac04-2708-56a0-a36f-f5e96e485251', 'word_count': 1000, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26f3ac04-2708-56a0-a36f-f5e96e485251'}, {'abstract': 'Our individualistic culture inflames the ego and numbs the spirit. Failure teaches us who we are.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/06/opinion/sunday/moral-revolution-david-brooks.html', 'snippet': 'Our individualistic culture inflames the ego and numbs the spirit. Failure teaches us who we are.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of the people I admire lead lives that have a two-mountain shape. They got out of school, began their career, started a family and identified the mountain they thought they were meant to climb — I’m going to be an entrepreneur, a doctor, a cop. They did the things society encourages us to do, like make a mark, become successful, buy a home, raise a family, pursue happiness.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07brooks/07brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 518, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07brooks/07brooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 518}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07brooks/07brooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07brooks/07brooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1767, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07brooks/07brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07brooks/07brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07brooks/07brooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Moral Peril of Meritocracy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Moral Peril of Meritocracy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-06T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fc0e40e-4f18-5f44-8e56-406cd040d422', 'word_count': 1644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fc0e40e-4f18-5f44-8e56-406cd040d422'}, {'abstract': 'This country will be a homeland for her in ways it never could be for an immigrant like me.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/06/opinion/sunday/immigration-parenting.html', 'snippet': 'This country will be a homeland for her in ways it never could be for an immigrant like me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For my entire adult life I’ve been trying to get back to the Europe I left in 1988 as a 9-year-old refugee from the Soviet Union. Get back there formally, once more with European passport in hand. No more statelessness for me, please.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07fishman/07fishman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07fishman/07fishman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 749}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07fishman/07fishman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 821, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07fishman/07fishman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1641, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07fishman/07fishman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07fishman/07fishman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/07/opinion/sunday/07fishman/07fishman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Daughter’s America — and Mine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Child’s America, and Mine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-06T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Boris Fishman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Boris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fishman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/46cecccb-92ad-5f12-b32c-1b393ec1d630', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46cecccb-92ad-5f12-b32c-1b393ec1d630'}, {'abstract': 'The message of inclusivity is meant to be helpful, but it can actually do harm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/06/opinion/sunday/women-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'The message of inclusivity is meant to be helpful, but it can actually do harm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'London — There is a giant mirror in my hometown in Ireland. It covers one side of a building that you must walk past to get from my mother’s house to the town center. When I was a teenager, I learned to take a different route. The mirror was always sparkling clean, a burst of reflection in the middle of a dull street. It showed me, abruptly, how others saw me.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07nolan/59b2b8d66e7346bca9a64b2752a4185f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07nolan/59b2b8d66e7346bca9a64b2752a4185f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 567}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07nolan/59b2b8d66e7346bca9a64b2752a4185f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 968, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07nolan/59b2b8d66e7346bca9a64b2752a4185f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 1456, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07nolan/07nolan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07nolan/07nolan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07nolan/07nolan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Do We All Have to Be Beautiful?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Don’t Have to Be Beautiful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-06T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/845c9bf5-fcaa-5553-b8ca-4d1aa049de78', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/845c9bf5-fcaa-5553-b8ca-4d1aa049de78'}, {'abstract': 'My usual method of packing involves reflecting on past moves and reliving the stress of each one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/06/sunday-review/why-i-hate-moving.html', 'snippet': 'My usual method of packing involves reflecting on past moves and reliving the stress of each one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUNICH — After six years in Germany, we are headed back home to California, and everyone asks me if I am using the Marie Kondo method to help me pack. I am actually using the lesser-known Firoozeh Dumas method, which involves spending half of each day remembering past moves, a lifetime total of 22 on three continents, and then reliving the stress of each one.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07dumas/f8240e3f7e964970950237912f65546f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 568, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07dumas/f8240e3f7e964970950237912f65546f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 568}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/08/opinion/sunday/07dumas/f8240e3f7e964970950237912f65546f-jumbo.jpg', 'height'