': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/09/health/fungus-microbiome-bowel-disease.html', 'snippet': 'Following extensive study of the body’s bacterial occupants, researchers are turning to how our fungal residents may contribute to inflammatory bowel diseases and other maladies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The connections among different parts of the human body are full of surprises, but here’s one you might not have considered: Could a thing that causes dandruff on your head also be contributing to your digestive problems?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/science/09FUNGI/merlin_153101826_ca00c2c0-e4be-411c-acf7-6a875714ddaa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/09/science/09FUNGI/merlin_153101826_ca00c2c0-e4be-411c-acf7-6a875714ddaa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/science/09FUNGI/merlin_153101826_ca00c2c0-e4be-411c-acf7-6a875714ddaa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/science/09FUNGI/merlin_153101826_ca00c2c0-e4be-411c-acf7-6a875714ddaa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/science/09FUNGI/merlin_153101826_ca00c2c0-e4be-411c-acf7-6a875714ddaa-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/09/science/09FUNGI/merlin_153101826_ca00c2c0