, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thaler, Richard H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Chris (1986- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-09T23:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b8ee8d3-e1d9-5969-927b-9d05e37045a7', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b8ee8d3-e1d9-5969-927b-9d05e37045a7'}, {'abstract': 'To fete the annual design fair, Studio Ossidiana turned the grounds of the Villa Necchi Campiglio into a fantastical spring garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/09/t-magazine/salone-del-mobile-party.html', 'snippet': 'To fete the annual design fair, Studio Ossidiana turned the grounds of the Villa Necchi Campiglio into a fantastical spring garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T’s annual Salone del Mobile celebration, which took place around the poppy-ringed swimming pool of the Villa Necchi Campiglio in Milan last night, was no ordinary garden party. As they drank Negronis, guests picked bouquets inside a hot pink stilted pavilion filled with alliums, thistles and lilies, wandered through a colonnade draped with swaths of Dedar fabric and bounced through an interactive step and repeat that evoked rolling turquoise hills — a fantastical landscape created by the Dutch design duo Studio Ossidiana. T’s editor in chief, Hanya Yanagihara, had invited the designers to bring the inventiveness of their recent Prix de Rome-winning project — in which they reimagined the Sixhaven area of Amsterdam as a floating playground — to the party (a model of that design was also on display inside the villa). “The idea was to turn it into a festival marking the beginning of spring,” Giovanni Bellotti, one of Ossidiana’s principals, said of the event. “And to reflect the springtime rituals around seeds and flowers that you see across different cultures,” added his partner, Alessandra Covini.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/design/t-salone-slide-8DGI/t-salone-slide-8DGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/design/t-salone-slide-8DGI/t-salone-slide-8DGI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/design/t-salone-slide-8DGI/t-salone-slide-8DGI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/design/t-salone-slide-8DGI/t-salone-slide-8DGI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/design/t-salone-slide-8DGI/t-salone-slide-8DGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/design/t-salone-slide-8DGI/t-salone-slide-8DGI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/t-magazine/design/t-salone-slide-8DGI/t-salone-slide-8DGI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'About Last Nigh