area controlled by a criminal paramilitary group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/10/world/americas/brazil-rio-caimans-favela.html', 'snippet': 'A storm knocked down the walls of a farm that bred caimans, cousins of alligators, in an area controlled by a criminal paramilitary group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The storm that swept through Rio de Janeiro this week left a wreck in its wake: A landslide swallowed homes, floodwaters rose up in hospitals and power lines collapsed as streets turned into roaring rivers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/10/world/10rio-flood1/merlin_153267429_e471944e-03c1-490a-bab3-73f8133c1ab1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/10/world/10rio-flood1/merlin_153267429_e471944e-03c1-490a-bab3-73f8133c1ab1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/10/world/10rio-flood1/merlin_153267429_e471944e-03c1-490a-bab3-73f8133c1ab1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/10/world/10rio-flood1/merlin_153267429_e471944e-03c1-490a-bab3-73f8133c1ab1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1404, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/10/world/10rio-flood1/10rio-flood1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/10/world/10rio-flood1/10rio-flood1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbna