ject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-10T21:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/500a760b-1fbe-504b-86ff-4b10cc37dac8', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/500a760b-1fbe-504b-86ff-4b10cc37dac8'}, {'abstract': 'Scripture offers at least two views of privacy: It’s necessary for a healthy spiritual life, but it also provides a place where sin can be committed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/10/opinion/sunday/privacy-religion.html', 'snippet': 'Scripture offers at least two views of privacy: It’s necessary for a healthy spiritual life, but it also provides a place where sin can be committed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the first interventions of God into human history, at least according to the Book of Genesis, relates to privacy. After God forbids Adam and Eve to eat the fruit of the “tree of knowledge,” the first couple do so anyway. As a result, they become aware that they are naked, clothe themselves with fig leaves and hide. When God asks why they are hiding, Adam responds, “I was afraid because I was naked.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/14/opinion/sunday/14Martin/a604aa782c4840d589ed3a839a945e26-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/14/opinion/sunday/14Martin/a604aa782c4840d589ed3a839a945e26-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 692}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/14/opinion/sunday/14Martin/a604aa782c4840d589ed3a839a945e26-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 888, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/14/opinion/sunday/14Martin/a604aa782c4840d589ed3a839a945e26-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1775, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/14/opinion/sunday/14Martin/14Martin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/14/opinion/sunday/14Martin/14Martin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/14/opinion/sunday/14Martin/14Martin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Bible Says About Secrets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bible Has Something to Say About Secrets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jesus Christ', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-10T21:38:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e4a04ad-f2b8-5d5e-9b5b-82f1bd1040d8', 'word_count': 1314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e4a04ad-f2b8-5d5e-9b5b-82f1bd1040d8'}, {'abstract': 'The president wants to limit the influence of state governments and the State Department in approving domestic and international pipelines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/10/business/energy-environment/trump-oil-gas-pipelines.html', 'snippet': 'The president wants to limit the influence of state governments and the State Department in approving domestic and international pipelines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — President Trump signed two executive orders on Wednesday that he says will speed up construction of pipelines and other projects to enhance the production and transport of oil and natural gas between states and across international borders.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/10/business/10pipe2/10pipe2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/10/business/10pipe2/10pipe2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/10/business/10pipe2/10pipe2-jumbo-v2.