s/girls-of-the-sun-review.html', 'snippet': 'Eva Husson’s ripped-from-real-life drama about Kurdish women fighting ISIS is a potent story marred by pompousness and good intentions.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Girls of the Sun,” Eva Husson’s ripped-from-real-life drama about a battalion of Kurdish women fighting the Islamic State in northern Iraq, begins and ends in the swirling dust of the same explosion. One survivor, a French journalist named Mathilde (Emmanuelle Bercot), becomes our guide and occasional narrator as she embeds with the unit and records the women’s stories.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/arts/girlsofthesun1/merlin_152986263_266a6d1b-e95d-429a-bd09-83b0ba5c8b78-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/09/arts/girlsofthesun1/merlin_152986263_266a6d1b-e95d-429a-bd09-83b0ba5c8b78-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/arts/girlsofthesun1/merlin_152986263_266a6d1b-e95d-429a-bd09-83b0ba5c8b78-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/arts/girlsofthesun1/merlin_152986263_266a6d1b-e95d-429a-bd09-83b0ba5c8b78-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/09/arts/girlsofthesun1/girlsofthesun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/09/arts