04/12/opinion/three-parent-babies-mitochondria.html', 'snippet': 'A procedure called mitochondrial replacement therapy could eliminate devastating diseases. It would not enable parents to ‘design’ their children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leigh syndrome is a terrible disease. In the worst cases, it emerges shortly after birth and claims one major organ after another. Movement becomes difficult, and then impossible. A tracheotomy and feeding tube are often necessary by toddlerhood, and as the disease progresses, lungs frequently have to be suctioned manually. Most children with the condition die by the age of 5 or 6.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12Mitochondria/12Mitochondria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12Mitochondria/12Mitochondria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12Mitochondria/12Mitochondria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12Mitochondria/12Mitochondria-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12Mitochondria/12Mitochondria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12Mitochondria/12Mitochondria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12Mitochondria/12Mitochondria-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Editorial Is Not About Designer Babies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Is Not About Designer Babies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'In Vitro Fertilization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mitochondria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academies of the United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-12T23:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c9fe12c-4db3-54ce-b89e-fe0d5c9972d4', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c9fe12c-4db3-54ce-b89e-fe0d5c9972d4'}, {'abstract': 'The good news about polarization is that it’s overstated — most Americans just really don’t like partisan squabbles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/12/opinion/polarization-politics-democrats-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'The good news about polarization is that it’s overstated — most Americans just really don’t like partisan squabbles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems that the only thing Americans can agree on is that we are living in an era of extreme political polarization. As we head into the 2020 presidential campaign, a striking 91 percent of people said in a recent PRRI survey that the country is divided over politics. This is higher than the percentage of people who reported that America is divided over issues of race and ethnicity (83 percent) or religion (77 percent).', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12klar-krupnikov-ryan/12klar-krupnikov-ryan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12klar-krupnikov-ryan/12klar-krupnikov-ryan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12klar-krupnikov-ryan/12klar-krupnikov-ryan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12klar-krupnikov-ryan/12klar-krupnikov-ryan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2040, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12klar-krupnikov-ryan/12klar-krupnikov-ryan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12klar-krupnikov-ryan/12klar-krupnikov-ryan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/12/opinion/12klar-krupnikov-ryan/12klar-krupnikov-ryan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLar