om/2019/04/13/crosswords/variety-acrostic.html', 'snippet': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon, there’s a universe inside your brains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ACROSTIC  — Today’s acrostic is one of the rare excerpts from a book that I have actually read, and recognize while solving, so I experienced that frisson of excitement you get when you spot a celebrity or see frolicking bobcats on a nature cam (which you can volunteer to do for science, from your own home). The nature reference here is intentional: Today’s author, Michael Pollan, has been an eloquent observer of humanity’s place in the natural world in books like “The Botany of Desire” and “The Omnivore’s Dilemma.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Acrostic', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-04-13T15:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ad08931-a20b-5a52-8e6a-114dc6acb019', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ad08931-a20b-5a52-8e6a-114dc6acb019'}, {'abstract': 'Crosby, who scored 100 points this season, has no points and only three shots on goal so far in the series, which now heads to Pittsburgh for Game 3 on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/13/sports/islanders-penguins-sidney-crosby.html', 'snippet': 'Crosby, who scored 100 points this season, has no points and only three shots on goal so far in the series, which now heads to Pittsburgh for Game 3 on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNIONDALE, N.Y. — The Islanders and their fierce checking have kept the Penguins’ high-scoring cap