as scarred by an extensive fire on Monday evening that caused its delicate spire to collapse, bruised the Parisian skies with smoke and further disheartened a city already back on its heels after weeks of violent protests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire Mauls Beloved Notre-Dame Cathedral in Paris', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fire Mauls Paris’s Beloved Notre-Dame', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Notre Dame Cathedral (Paris, France)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-15T17:27:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter and Aurelien Breeden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Aurelien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Breeden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff9832f9-c755-5a0c-8997-f530c44f33ef', 'word_count': 1449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff9832f9-c755-5a0c-8997-f530c44f33ef'}, {'abstract': 'Alison Roman’s creamy cauliflower pasta used to be something she just made for herself. You’ll want to hoard it, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/15/dining/cauliflower-pasta-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Alison Roman’s creamy cauliflower pasta used to be something she just made for herself. You’ll want to hoard it, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While I consider nearly every meal I make an opportunity for recipe development, sometimes the food I cook for myself at home when nobody is watching is, well, not very impressive. It can feel too simple, too beige or too boring to ever see the light of day. I lovingly refer to those dishes as “personal dinners.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15roman1/merlin_153434439_3c3ca825-6839-4984-80d3-3005c503c162-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15roman1/merlin_153434439_3c3ca825-6839-4984-80d3-3005c503c162-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15roman1/merlin_153434439_3c3ca825-6839-4984-80d3-3005c503c162-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15roman1/merlin_153434439_3c3ca825-6839-4984-80d3-3005c503c162-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1489, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15roman1/15roman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15roman1/15roman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15roman1/15roman1