-ad5e556f2639'}, {'abstract': 'Nasoya’s new line of kimchis are mild and spicy, and every one is vegan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/15/dining/vegan-kimchi.html', 'snippet': 'Nasoya’s new line of kimchis are mild and spicy, and every one is vegan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So you thought that Korean kimchi, made from ingredients like Napa cabbage and radishes, was vegan? Not necessarily, as there’s most likely some fish sauce lurking in the mix. Nasoya, a company that specializes in tofu and other vegetarian Asian products, has introduced fishless vegan kimchi in four styles: regular spicy Napa cabbage, mild Napa cabbage, mild white Napa cabbage and a ruddy mild radish variety.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner4/15burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner4/15burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner4/15burner4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner4/15burner4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1527, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner4/15burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner4/15burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner4/15burner4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vegan Kimchis to Savor', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Complement: Vegan Kimchis Ignore the Fish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kimchi (South Korean Food)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veganism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nasoya Foods USA LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-15T22:58:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1af1d3f-6f80-546a-8e3f-c24d003dffc7', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1af1d3f-6f80-546a-8e3f-c24d003dffc7'}, {'abstract': 'The G.O.P. could really use a remarkably successful policy entrepreneur.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/15/opinion/bernie-sanders-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'The G.O.P. could really use a remarkably successful policy entrepreneur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Bernie Sanders released the latest version of his “Medicare for all” plan, which would establish a federally run single-payer system to finance care for everyone in the United States. The plan has changed little from its previous iterations, but there is one crucial difference: This version is backed by several of Mr. Sanders’s rivals for the Democratic presidential nomination.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/opinion/16Suderman/16Suderman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/16/opinion/16Suderman/16Suderman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/opinion/16Suderman/16Suderman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/opinion/16Suderman/16Suderman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/opinion/16Suderman/16Suderman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/16/opinion/16Suderman/16Suderman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/opinion/16Suderman/16Suderman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bernie Sanders Has an Important Lesson for Republicans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Can Learn From Sanders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cato Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Progressive Caucus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jayapal, Pramila', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-15T23:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Suderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/382a0897-95a1-597a-8ccf-b5d03759d7b0', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/382a0897-95a1-597a-8ccf-b5d03759d7b0'}, {'abstract': 'Hangar 1 has ventured beyond just vodka distilling with a brandy named for a classic airplane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/15/dining/drinks/bentwing-brandy.html', 'snippet': 'Hangar 1 has ventured beyond just vodka distilling with a brandy named for a classic airplane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hangar 1, the vodka distiller, is in a repurposed airplane hangar on Alameda Island in San Francisco Bay, where Navy planes, including one called the Bent-Wing Bird, were housed. The spirits company has taken that name for its latest product, its first that’s not a vodka. The brandy is a blend of French and California spirits, aged in charred whiskey barrels. It has a floral bouquet and takes flight on the palate, with honey, vanilla and golden raisin notes. As brandies go, it’s more delicate than bold.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner2/15burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner2/15burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 983}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner2/15burner2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner2/15burner2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1250, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner2/15burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner2/15burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner2/15burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Brandy Soars', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: This Brandy Is Set to Soar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vodka', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hangar 1 Distillery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALAMEDA COUNTY (CALIF)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-15T23:06:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0314cf8-68f2-5548-8f97-37c9a4fd061f', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0314cf8-68f2-5548-8f97-37c9a4fd061f'}, {'abstract': 'Made In’s new carbon-steel wok has a flat bottom to accommodate home kitchens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/15/dining/carbon-steel-wok-made-in.html', 'snippet': 'Made In’s new carbon-steel wok has a flat bottom to accommodate home kitchens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Made In, the company that manufactures cookware and ships it directly to consumers, has added a roomy carbon-steel wok to its line. It’s hefty and heats quickly, with a generous handle that stays cool. A flattened bottom allows it to be used on a home stove. It requires seasoning before it’s used the first time. Made In recently announced that Grant Achatz and Nick Kokonas of the Alinea Group in Chicago have joined Tom Colicchio on its advisory board. The Alinea Group is now stocking its kitchens with Made In equipment.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner5/15burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner5/15burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner5/15burner5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner5/15burner5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1444, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner5/15burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner5/15burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner5/15burner5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Wok Will Sit on Your Stovetop', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Stir-Fry: A Wok That’s Fit For the Stovetop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steel and Iron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Made In Cookware', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-15T23:08:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bafc77e8-bbad-5292-8b32-82c95fae0b62', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bafc77e8-bbad-5292-8b32-82c95fae0b62'}, {'abstract': '‘Happiness Is Baking’ has favorite recipes from the 102-year-old baker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/15/dining/maida-heatter-cookbook.html', 'snippet': '‘Happiness Is Baking’ has favorite recipes from the 102-year-old baker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I first met Maida Heatter in 1982, at a party at the home of Craig Claiborne, a former New York Times food editor. She had baked batches of her pecan squares Americana, a recipe included in her first cookbook. We hit it off, and I visited her at her home in Miami Beach on a number of occasions. She is now 102 years old and has very few visitors. There’s a new collection of her top recipes assembled from her many cookbooks, with her blessing. Not just the pecan squares, but also some of my favorites like the East 62nd Street lemon cake, Countess Toulouse-Lautrec’s French chocolate cake and rugelach. In her meticulous instructions, she often refers to using the large bowl of an electric mixer. That’s because she owned a Sunbeam, the pre-KitchenAid appliance of choice, which came with bowls in two sizes. Paintings illustrate many of the recipes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner3/15burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 256, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner3/15burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 256}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/dining/15burner3/15burner3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 