Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-16T17:17:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niraj Chokshi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niraj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chokshi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/417703b7-8b71-5f07-bd09-0a9461aaaf89', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/417703b7-8b71-5f07-bd09-0a9461aaaf89'}, {'abstract': 'After President Trump attacked the freshman Democrat from Minnesota on Twitter, Democrats pushed back. But they are choosing their words with caution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/16/us/politics/ilhan-omar-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'After President Trump attacked the freshman Democrat from Minnesota on Twitter, Democrats pushed back. But they are choosing their words with caution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When President Trump tweeted an edited video portraying Representative Ilhan Omar as playing down the 9/11 attacks, it took less than three hours for Senator Bernie Sanders to rush to her defense and declare her “a leader with strength and courage.” But when a Fox News anchor described Mr. Sanders on Monday night as “a staunch supporter” of Ms. Omar, the senator balked.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/us/politics/16dc-omar/merlin_148393167_4d04efef-84a0-4fb2-b1f8-2e87b416d74d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/16/us/politics/16dc-omar/merlin_148393167_4d04efef-84a0-4fb2-b1f8-2e87b416d74d-articleLarge.j