s cathedral of Notre-Dame in Paris, the last Mass of the day was underway on Monday of Holy Week when the first fire alarm went off. It was 6:20 p.m., 25 minutes before the heavy wooden doors were scheduled to close to visitors for the day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notre-Dame Attic Was Known as ‘the Forest.’ And It Burned Like One.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Forest’ of Parched Timber, and Little to Stop a Blaze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Notre Dame Cathedral (Paris, France)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-16T22:23:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aurelien Breeden, Elian Peltier, Liz Alderman and Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aurelien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Breeden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peltier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30ed4ecd-8a76-57f9-9053-218a7b5aa562', 'word_count': 1529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30ed4ecd-8a76-57f9-9053-218a7b5aa562'}, {'abstract': 'The case, involving a Human Rights Watch worker, tests the boundaries of criticism and protest in Israel. The advocacy group will appeal to Israel’s Supreme Court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/16/world/middleeast/israel-boycott-deport-hrw.html', 'snippet': 'The case, involving a Human Rights Watch worker, tests the boundaries of criticism and protest in Israel. The advocacy group will appeal to Israel’s Supreme Court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — An advocate for Human Rights Watch must leave the country by May 1, an Israeli court ruled on Tuesday, upholding a deportation order issued under a contentious law that bars entry to foreigners who have publicly called for a boycott of Israel or its settlements in the occupied West Bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/world/16israel-HRW/merlin_137891325_94159472-e7a9-483c-b43c-5c3cfb01c8d2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/16/world/16israel-HRW/merlin_137891325_94159472-e7a9-483c-b43c-5c3cfb01c8d2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/world/16israel-HRW/merlin_137891325_94159472-e7a9-483c-b43c-5c3cfb01c8d2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/world/16israel-HRW/merlin_137891325_94159472-e7a9-483c-b43c-5c3cfb01c8d2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1323, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/16/world/16israel-HRW/16