ject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-17T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hartosh Singh Bal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hartosh', 'middlename': 'Singh', 'lastname': 'Bal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4faac90a-7cc2-5a22-b3c3-526c1da0f605', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4faac90a-7cc2-5a22-b3c3-526c1da0f605'}, {'abstract': 'Funding for the Special Olympics may have been restored, but many more important programs are still on the chopping block.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/17/opinion/disability-budget-cuts-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Funding for the Special Olympics may have been restored, but many more important programs are still on the chopping block.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month’s proposal from Secretary of Education Betsy DeVos to cut millions of dollars in funding for Special Olympics caused a public uproar and a bipartisan backlash fierce enough to force President Trump to restore it days later. That reversal was welcome. But it was also incomplete. Most Americans do not know that the 2020 budget is still full of cuts that aim directly at many other programs that support people with disabilities. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/17/opinion/17Ridge/17Ridge-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/17/opinion/17Ridge/17Rid