to elaborate conspiracy theories. In a lengthy deposition video, a lawyer pushes him steadily back toward facts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five days after Attorney General William Barr released his expectation-deflating summary of the investigation into the Trump campaign’s suspected Russia connections, a pair of videos appeared on YouTube, labeled “Alex Jones / Sandy Hook Video Deposition.” The hundreds of thousands of views those videos have accumulated attest to their appeal as a #Resistance consolation prize: Maybe it’s not a habitually lying president, but at least someone is getting called to account, under oath, for his role in the post-truthification of American public life.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-screenland/21mag-screenland-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-screenland/21mag-screenland-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-screenland/21mag-screenland-jumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-screenland/21mag-screenland-superJumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-screenland/21mag-screenland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-screenland/21mag-screenland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-screenland/21mag-screenland-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Jones Under Oath Is an Antidote to a ‘Post-Truth’ Age', 'kicker': 'Screenland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Third Degree', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Alex (1974- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infowars', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sandy Hook Elementary School (Newtown, Conn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-17T13:01:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Homans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Homans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60bd02ca-67b8-5800-b50a-6f8257a4fe76', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60bd02ca-67b8-5800-b50a-6f8257a4fe76'}, {'abstract': 'In three decades of advocating for prison abolition, the activist and scholar has helped transform how people think about criminal justice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/17/magazine/prison-abolition-ruth-wilson-gilmore.html', 'snippet': 'In three decades of advocating for prison abolition, the activist and scholar has helped transform how people think about criminal justice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s an anecdote that Ruth Wilson Gilmore likes to share about being at an environmental-justice conference in Fresno in 2003. People from all over California’s Central Valley had gathered to talk about the serious environmental hazards their communities faced, mostly as a result of decades of industrial farming, conditions that still have not changed. (The air quality in the Central Valley is the worst in the nation, and one million of its residents drink tap water more poisoned than the water in Flint, Mich.) There was a “youth track” at the conference, in which children were meant to talk about their worries and then decide as a group what was most important to be done in the name of environmental justice. Gilmore, a renowned geography professor (then at University of California, Berkeley, now at the CUNY Graduate Center in Manhattan) and an influential figure in the prison-abolition movement, was a keynote speaker.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '37', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-gilmore-hppromo/21mag-gilmore-hppromo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-gilmore-hppromo/21mag-gilmore-hppromo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 705}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-gilmore-hppromo/21mag-gilmore-hppromo-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 872, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/magazine/21mag-gilmore-hppromo/21mag-gilmore-hppromo-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1743, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 