 in May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cannes Film Festival on Thursday unveiled a set of movies in contention for this year’s Palme d’Or. The American director Terrence Malick — who won in 2011 for “The Tree of Life” — is back with “A Hidden Life,” set during World War II. Films by Pedro Almodóvar of Spain and Ken Loach of Britain are also in the running.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/20/world/18cannes-itel-sub/merlin_138003000_229a9370-4ec4-46a3-b8b5-2d63935172f6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/20/world/18cannes-itel-sub/merlin_138003000_229a9370-4ec4-46a3-b8b5-2d63935172f6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/20/world/18cannes-itel-sub/merlin_138003000_229a9370-4ec4-46a3-b8b5-2d63935172f6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/20/world/18cannes-itel-sub/merlin_138003000_229a9370-4ec4-46a3-b8b5-2d63935172f6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/20/world/18cannes-itel-sub/18cannes-itel-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/20/world/18cannes-itel-sub/18cannes-itel-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':