 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69b8ed5e-0f99-5469-9a5e-61f1631ba1cd', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b8ed5e-0f99-5469-9a5e-61f1631ba1cd'}, {'abstract': 'Almost every object I encounter is mass-produced — must my face be too?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/18/opinion/instagram-celebrity-plastic-surgery.html', 'snippet': 'Almost every object I encounter is mass-produced — must my face be too?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take a look at the most beautiful of today’s top Instagram influencers and they all look astoundingly the same — their butts, perfect bouncing balloons; the smooth curves of their itty-bitty waists; lips pursed into a big swollen pout, with contoured noses, sharp cheekbones, and smoldering bedroom eyes. The Instagram ideal beauty standard is embodied by Kim Kardashian and Kylie Jenner — a sexy baby meets Jessica Rabbit — and it falls a smidge to the right of the pit of the uncanny valley. As many devoted Instagram accounts reveal, it’s a look that takes a lot of cosmetic work and digital alteration to achieve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/opinion/18peyser2/merlin_146293722_dd492fa3-cba5-46d3-9965-e412a1bf7d04-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/18/opinion/18peyser2/merlin_146293722_dd492fa3-cba5-46d3-9965-e412a1bf7d04-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/opinion/18peyser2/merlin_146293722_dd492fa3-cba5-46d3-9965-e412a1bf7d04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/op