r/18leonhardt-newsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/opinion/18leonhardt-newsletter/18leonhardt-newsletter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Civil-Rights Movement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-18T13:13:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0df8bb09-70b3-58e6-8ac5-214fbbf4284a', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0df8bb09-70b3-58e6-8ac5-214fbbf4284a'}, {'abstract': 'High above Manhattan, Alicja Kwade’s planetary sculpture captures the music of the spheres.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/18/arts/design/met-roof-garden-alicja-kwade.html', 'snippet': 'High above Manhattan, Alicja Kwade’s planetary sculpture captures the music of the spheres.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, when I looked at the first image ever made of a black hole — erroneously called a “photograph,” it is in fact a digital composition stitched together from the observations of eight telescopes — I could hardly make it out. The supermassive void at the heart of the Messier 87 galaxy is about as large as our solar system, with a mass outstripping the sun’s more than 6 billion times over, from which no light escapes. What the picture shows is the event horizon that surrounds it, an aureole of blazing fire; but the halo appears blurry and indistinct, and within seconds it had been repurposed for all manner of pathetic digital jokes. Try to capture the infinitude of space and this is what you get: a fall from grace, a descent from the heavens to earth.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/19/arts/19metrooftop/merlin_153641469_224bbe8a-c797-4f4c-bc2d-3188bdc1cbfa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/19/arts/19metrooftop/merlin_153641469_224bbe8a-c797-4f4c-bc2d-3188bdc1cbfa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/19/arts/19metrooftop/merlin_153641469_224bbe8a-c797-4f4c-bc2d-3188bdc1cbfa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/19/arts/19metrooftop/merlin_153641469_224bbe8a-c797-4f4c-bc2d-3188bdc1cbfa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/19/arts/19metrooftop/17metrooftop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/19/arts/19metrooftop/17metrooftop-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/19/arts/19metrooftop/17metrooftop-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celestial Visions on the Met Roof', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Sculptor Puts the Soul In Solar System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kwade, Alicja', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-18T13:23:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Farago', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farago', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/19735a42-dafa-59b3-bd23-051356eead7e', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19735a42-dafa-59b3-bd23-051356eead7e'}, {'abstract': 'More adults are living with their parents, but home prices may not be the only thing driving that trend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/18/realestate/where-are-adults-living-with-their-parents.html', 'snippet': 'More adults are living with their parents, but home prices may not be the only thing driving that trend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A frequently referenced 2016 Pew Research Center report found that, across the country, more adults are living with their parents — about 15 percent of those between the ages of 25 and 35. In 2000, that figure was 10 percent, and in 1981 it was just 8 percent. The ever-increasing cost of housing is an obvious factor, but it may not be the only one. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/realestate/18calculator-1555431551993/18calculator-1555431551993-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/18/realestate/18calculator-1555431551993/18calculator-1555431551993-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/realestate/18calculator-1555431551993/18calculator-1555431551993-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/realestate/18calculator-1555431551993/18calculator-1555431551993-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/realestate/18calculator-1555431551993/18calculator-1555431551993-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/18/realestate/18calculator-1555431551993/18calculator-1555431551993-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201