b'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department released a redacted version of the special counsel’s report on Thursday. Times reporters uncovered the biggest findings and shared excerpts and analysis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/18/us/politics/the-mueller-report-excerpts.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department released a redacted version of the special counsel’s report on Thursday. Times reporters uncovered the biggest findings and shared excerpts and analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a sweeping, 22-month investigation, Robert S. Mueller III found there was insufficient evidence to establish that President Trump or his associates engaged in a criminal conspiracy with Russia to disrupt the 2016 election, despite numerous contacts between his campaign and Russians. Mr. Mueller’s report also detailed the president’s efforts to thwart the investigation, and the investigators debated whether the episodes amounted to criminal obstruction of justice. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpts and Analysis From the Mueller Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mueller Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, William P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGahn, Donald F II', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Prosecutors (Independent Counsel)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-18T15:24:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5b3f88d-fb5a-5394-ae9d-3ac54e361502', 'word_count': 4025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5b3f88d-fb5a-5394-ae9d-3ac54e361502'}, {'abstract': 'Our journalists in Washington discuss what the report means and what may come next.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/18/reader-center/robert-mueller-investigation-questions.html', 'snippet': 'Our journalists in Washington discuss what the report means and what may come next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost two years after the Mueller investigation began, the special counsel’s findings, submitted last month, have become public. On Thursday, Attorney General William P. Barr released a redacted version of the more than 400-page report. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/us/politics/18dc-readerqa/merlin_153685680_494fba67-209f-4109-b1c2-d8db0ea6a68c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/18/us/politics/18dc-readerqa/merlin_153685680_494fba67-209f-4109-b1c2-d8db0ea6a68c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/18/us/politics/18dc-readerqa/merlin_153685680_494fba67-209f-4109-b1c2-d8db0ea6a68c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 