cal? What is the appeal of the fakely found? The frame for Jonathan Carr’s whopper of a debut novel purports to be an “extract from ‘Chicago: An Alternative History 1800-1900’ by Professor Milton Winship, University of Chicago, A. C. McClurg & Co., 1902.” This sprawling book’s chronological vignettes map a “leisurely journey” through the 19th century as pastiched from ostensible sources: newspaper articles, journal entries, letters, notes for an exhibition of photographs, even a review of the history book itself.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/books/review/19Rooney/19Rooney-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 489, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/21/books/review/19Rooney/19Rooney-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 489}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/books/review/19Rooney/19Rooney-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/books/review/19Rooney/19Rooney-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 1676, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/books/review/19Rooney/19Rooney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/21/books/review/19Rooney/19Rooney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/books/review/19Rooney/1