, 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b9068c7-0429-5840-aa8a-1327ce8ea93d', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b9068c7-0429-5840-aa8a-1327ce8ea93d'}, {'abstract': 'Born and bred in Bedford-Stuyvesant and now living in Park Slope, the performer likes to slow down the pace on the weekends with yoga, meditation and time with her dog, Jeremiah.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/19/nyregion/bette-smith-soul-singer-sunday-routine.html', 'snippet': 'Born and bred in Bedford-Stuyvesant and now living in Park Slope, the performer likes to slow down the pace on the weekends with yoga, meditation and time with her dog, Jeremiah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Saturday night at the performance space Littlefield in Gowanus, Brooklyn, the singer Bette Smith moved effortlessly across the stage wearing a tight holographic vinyl dress and five-inch-heeled thigh-high boots, strutting like Tina Turner. Since her start at age 5 singing in church, Ms. Smith has performed at the Montreux Jazz Festival in Switzerland and toured Europe multiple times. She is currently on tour in Spain. But when Ms. Smith is in New York, she spends her Sundays meditating, volunteering and taking hot yoga classes. She lives in Park Slope, Brooklyn, with her Australian Labradoodle, Jeremiah.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE1/21ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE1/21ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE1/21ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE1/21ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE1/21ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE1/21ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE1/21ROUTINE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Bette Smith, Soul Singer, Spends Her Sundays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yoga, Some Cooking and a Lot of Soul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Bette (Singer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meditation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-19T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Enman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Enman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de78d396-b367-515c-99da-59261eea741a', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de78d396-b367-515c-99da-59261eea741a'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks could be a superteam next season. Or their owner, James L. Dolan, could mess it all up. What’s a fan to believe?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/19/sports/knicks-durant-kyrie-dolan.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks could be a superteam next season. Or their owner, James L. Dolan, could mess it all up. What’s a fan to believe?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another wretched Knicks season has ended, but from its ashes a justifiable optimism is taking root. The Knicks have the money to add two star players this summer, and there is a growing buzz in the N.B.A. that they could acquire Kevin Durant of the Golden State Warriors and Kyrie Irving of the Boston Celtics, who can be free agents.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/22/sports/22-DOLAN-01-PRINT/merlin_153658827_18e3b179-49c7-429c-9e62-c3dff9a5f9bb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/22/sports/22-DOLAN-01-PRINT/merlin_153658827_18e3b179-49c7-429c-9e62-c3dff9a5f9bb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/22/sports/22-DOLAN-01-PRINT/merlin_153658827_18e3b179-49c7-429c-9e62-c3dff9a5f9bb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '