e', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/eaeeb88d-82e6-5d0f-a8fc-8b2b4e00abe4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/eaeeb88d-82e6-5d0f-a8fc-8b2b4e00abe4'}, {'abstract': 'Lewis’s seven-part series examines our relationship to authority and to regulation — our mistrust of them and, in some cases, our full-throated hostility toward them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/19/books/review-michael-lewis-podcast-against-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Lewis’s seven-part series examines our relationship to authority and to regulation — our mistrust of them and, in some cases, our full-throated hostility toward them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Storytelling is a hell of a skill. Michael Lewis has used it to make nonspecialist readers not just pick up but tear through books about baseball talent scouting, collateralized debt obligation and the intricacies of government bureaucracy. Lewis is famous because he makes people feel like they understand, however briefly, an overly complex world.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/03/books/review/03BOOKLEWIS2/03BOOKLEWIS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/03/books/review/03BOOKLEWIS2/03BOOKLEWIS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/03/books/review/03BOOKLEWIS2/03BOOKLEWIS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/03/books/review/03BOOKLEWIS2/03BOOKLEWIS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1477, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':