ards of Hope in Mozambique', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mozambique', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyclones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-20T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6650f3b-d470-550a-8ec7-d835e52b7156', 'word_count': 1435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6650f3b-d470-550a-8ec7-d835e52b7156'}, {'abstract': 'The soul of France. Disappearing glaciers. The most chaotic place on the internet. Bauhaus at 100. And more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/20/arts/11-of-our-best-weekend-reads.html', 'snippet': 'The soul of France. Disappearing glaciers. The most chaotic place on the internet. Bauhaus at 100. And more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to the weekend. To say it’s been a busy news week may be a small understatement. We began with devastating news out of Paris as a fire ravaged the Notre-Dame cathedral and ended with the release of the redacted Mueller report. For those celebrating this weekend, we hope you enjoy your holiday and some great reads along the way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cre