soba sauce, with a soy-sauce base and plenty of umami, to toss on the needle-thin buckwheat pasta, served hot or cold.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner4/22burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner4/22burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 757}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner4/22burner4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 812, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner4/22burner4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1624, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner4/22burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner4/22burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner4/22burner4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Source for Soba at Home', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Dress: A New Source For Soba at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noodles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japanese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sobaya (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-22T20:19:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1070e8f-84f7-5404-ba4d-671a31c2d1ca', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1070e8f-84f7-5404-ba4d-671a31c2d1ca'}, {'abstract': 'Three Owls Market in the West Village of Manhattan stocks prepared foods to eat in or take away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/22/dining/three-owls-market.html', 'snippet': 'Three Owls Market in the West Village of Manhattan stocks prepared foods to eat in or take away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suzanne Dumaine — a trained chef, recipe developer and writer — is flying solo at her own West Village grocery and cafe, Three Owls Market. She’s stocking the shelves with items that look to Italy, like pastas, cheeses, olive oils, sauces and a small selection of everyday food staples. Chickens raised in the Catskills are burnished on a rotisserie. There are prepared dishes like broccoli with gremolata, Negroni-cured salmon tartine and porchetta, to take away or to order at a counter all day and evening, and tables set to one side of the double storefront. As for the name, she said it relates to a bedtime story about three owls that her father used to tell her.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/24/dining/22burner5/merlin_153698625_0ff3c98d-78