one, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/22/well/well-gay/well-gay-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1796, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/22/well/well-gay/well-gay-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/22/well/well-gay/well-gay-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/22/well/well-gay/well-gay-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Gay Are You?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-23T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd870b27-d80c-5521-98df-12ba2df0a87e', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd870b27-d80c-5521-98df-12ba2df0a87e'}, {'abstract': 'You might want to consider taping your mouth shut at night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/23/magazine/how-to-be-a-nose-breather.html', 'snippet': 'You might want to consider taping your mouth shut at night.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘‘Start by being cognizant of your breathing patterns during the day,” says Nicholas Michalak, chief executive at Somnifix, a company that sells adhesive strips for people who want to tape their mouths shut at night to enforce nose breathing. Set alarms on your phone throughout the day to check in and remind yourself to use your nostrils. Humans naturally do most of their breathing through their nasal passages, which serve to heat, humidify and filter the air. It’s not uncommon, though, to slip into a mouth-breathing habit. Test yourself by inhaling through your nostrils. If you can’t, you may have some kind of obstruction, and should go see an ear, nose and throat specialist. If you can but tend not to, you may be an accidental mouth breather.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-Tip-1/28mag-Tip-1-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 567, 'width': 567, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-Tip-1/28mag-Tip-1-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 567, 'width': 567, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-Tip-1/28mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-Tip-1/28mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-Tip-1/28mag-T