2c88c30', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f6e39c9-287f-5825-853f-31b032c88c30'}, {'abstract': 'How Western liberalism’s peculiar relationship to its Christian heritage leaves non-Western Christians exposed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/23/opinion/sri-lanka-bombing-christians.html', 'snippet': 'How Western liberalism’s peculiar relationship to its Christian heritage leaves non-Western Christians exposed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The murderous radicals who set off bombs and killed hundreds on Easter Sunday in Sri Lanka chose their targets with ideological purpose. Three churches were bombed, and with them three hotels catering to Western tourists, because often in the jihadist imagination Western Christianity and Western liberal individualism are the conjoined enemies of their longed-for religious utopia, their religious-totalitarian version of Islam. Tourists and missionaries, Coca-Cola and the Catholic Church — it’s all the same invading Christian enemy, different brand names for the same old crusade. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/23douthatWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/23douthatWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/23douthatWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23douthatWeb/23douthatWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbn