'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b8c1ec7-b145-5c3e-be05-b0c6347c2d03', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b8c1ec7-b145-5c3e-be05-b0c6347c2d03'}, {'abstract': 'The strongest pushback against the president came from his own branch of government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/23/opinion/mueller-report-trump-white-house-resitance.html', 'snippet': 'The strongest pushback against the president came from his own branch of government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly everyone interprets the exhaustive, nearly 450-page report from Robert Mueller as a story of presidential overreach. Convinced that Mr. Mueller’s investigation would embarrass his administration by revealing the extent of Russian influence on the 2016 election, President Trump attempted to undermine the special counsel’s probe. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23posner-hemel/23posner-hemel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23posner-hemel/23posner-hemel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23posner-hemel/23posner-hemel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/opinion/23posner-hemel/23posner-hemel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 2048, '