'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f6d8e84b-fec7-5c39-872f-a491c022d688', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f6d8e84b-fec7-5c39-872f-a491c022d688'}, {'abstract': 'Iron Man, Thor, the Hulk, Captain America and other stars settle scores, tie up loose ends and take a long victory lap in the final chapter of this cycle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/23/movies/avengers-endgame-review.html', 'snippet': 'Iron Man, Thor, the Hulk, Captain America and other stars settle scores, tie up loose ends and take a long victory lap in the final chapter of this cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': '“No amount of money ever bought a second of time,” one character says to another — I’m afraid I can’t be any more specific than that — somewhere around the middle of “Avengers: Endgame.” So true, so true, and also in context so completely not true. The intersecting axes of time and money are what this franchise is all about, and while I’m not an expert in studio math, I’d guess that a second of the movie, based on what Disney and Marvel Studios paid to make it, would buy a decent used car.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/arts/23avengers-hp-promo/23avengers-hp-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/23/arts/23avengers-hp-promo/23avengers-hp-promo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/23/arts/23avengers-hp-promo/23avengers-hp-promo-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy'