b324f-2af7-599a-996d-163e9aa586bd'}, {'abstract': 'Athletes who pass return-to-play tests after an A.C.L. injury remain just as likely to experience a subsequent knee injury as those who fail the tests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/24/well/move/after-a-knee-injury-be-wary-when-returning-to-sports.html', 'snippet': 'Athletes who pass return-to-play tests after an A.C.L. injury remain just as likely to experience a subsequent knee injury as those who fail the tests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Athletes who have torn an anterior cruciate knee ligament often rely on elaborate batteries of physical tests to tell them if and when they are ready to return to competitive sports. But a new review of studies of athletes and A.C.L. injuries raises serious concerns about the reliability of these return-to-play tests.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/well/physed-knee/merlin_50399769_2ede1635-bbe3-4875-8f9c-fed589342dc7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/30/well/physed-knee/merlin_50399769_2ede1635-bbe3-4875-8f9c-fed589342dc7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/well/physed-knee/merlin_50399769_2ede1635-bbe3-4875-8f9c-fed589342dc7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/well/physed-knee/merlin_50399769_2ede1635-bbe3-4875-8f9c-fed589342dc7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/well/physed-knee/physed-knee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/30/well/physed-knee/physed-knee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/30/well/physed-knee/physed-knee-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Knee Injury, Be Wary When Returning to Sports', 'kicker': 'Phys Ed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Knee Is Good to Go. Oh, Really?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-24T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2f2c287-c6c5-5648-86e4-ee06cd259a97', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2f2c287-c6c5-5648-86e4-ee06cd259a97'}, {'abstract': 'They were the movies most interested in how ordinary people connect. And they’re essentially gone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/24/magazine/romantic-comedy-movies.html', 'snippet': 'They were the movies most interested in how ordinary people connect. And they’re essentially gone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have a confession to make: I miss Katherine Heigl. In the mid- to late 2000s she spent five years doing romantic comedies, or what was left of them by the time she got there. She put up a decent fight. To watch her withstand the jeers of the boy-men in “Knocked Up,” the cave-manning of Gerard Butler in “The Ugly Truth” or the bridesmaid-outfit montage in “27 Dresses” was to witness a genre’s assault on one of its last dedicated practitioners. Heigl didn’t get to show the luminance, flintiness or idiosyncrasy of her romantic-comedy forebears; she was given too few moments of wit or insight. Instead, she was tough, stubborn, gainfully employed and — like most of the women in these movies, by that point — counterproductively heartless, tolerant of whatever partnership the plot backed her into. Her time as a romantic-comedy star was more a feat of survival than a cause for celebration. But as long as Heigl was around, so were romantic comedies, and that was something.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-comedies-promo/28mag-comedies-promo-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-comedies-promo/28mag-comedies-promo-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-comedies-promo/28mag-comedies-promo-jumbo.png', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-comedies-promo/28mag-comedies-promo-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-comedies-promo/28mag-comedies-promo-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-comedies-promo/28mag-comedies-promo-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-comedies-promo/28mag-comedies-promo-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rom-Coms Were Corny and Retrograde. Why Do I Miss Them so Much?', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twilight of The Romcoms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heigl, Katherine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Meg', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sex and the City (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'When Harry Met Sally (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-24T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wesley Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8b78e41-8ba8-5cc1-b736-dcb77ff85c59', 'word_count': 3849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8b78e41-8ba8-5cc1-b736-dcb77ff85c59'}, {'abstract': 'How does a restaurant get to 30 years? Maybe by cooking true and delicious food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/24/magazine/honest-recipes-like-this-beef-carpaccio-will-never-go-out-of-style.html', 'snippet': 'How does a restaurant get to 30 years? Maybe by cooking true and delicious food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prune turns the big 20 this year — which is, we often joke, actually 140 when counted in fiercely competitive and fickle restaurant years, where one can go from sizzle-hot to morgue-cold in a New York minute. I’ve been reflective about making it this far, which is to be expected, but I’ve surprised myself by how overearnest we’ve sometimes become. Who have we been and what have we accomplished and what have we meant and to whom have we mattered? I’ve found myself wondering, with bloated self-regard, perhaps unwittingly swept up in the current cultural moment the restaurant industry is having?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373/28mag-eat-slideshow-slide-G373-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Honest Recipes, Like This Beef Carpaccio, Will Never Go Out of Style', 'kicker': 'Eat ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honest Recipes, Like This Beef Carpaccio, Will Never Go Out of Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potatoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beef', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-24T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc8a94a-efc4-57d2-a998-5126318472b8', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc8a94a-efc4-57d2-a998-5126318472b8'}, {'abstract': 'A lot of would-be presidents are clever people. Few have a cleverness so well targeted toward liberal intellectuals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/24/magazine/pete-buttigieg-smart-harvard-rhodes-scholar-norwegian-language.html', 'snippet': 'A lot of would-be presidents are clever people. Few have a cleverness so well targeted toward liberal intellectuals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late this March, a Norwegian news outlet sprang a surprise question on Pete Buttigieg, the mayor of South Bend, Ind., and candidate for president. The previous week, the writer Anand Giridharadas, who has close to half a million Twitter followers, tweeted that he met Buttigieg and introduced him to a Norwegian friend. “Instantaneously,” he wrote, “Mayor Pete starts talking to her in Norwegian, like a magic trick.” Apparently Buttigieg had read a Norwegian novel in translation and been so taken by it that he learned the language just to finish the author’s untranslated works.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-2/28mag-screenland-2-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-2/28mag-screenland-2-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-2/28mag-screenland-2-jumbo.png', 'height': 791, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/magazine/28mag-screenland-2/28mag-screenland-2-superJumbo.png', 'height': 791, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {