rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alliance Defending Freedom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Employment Opportunity Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RG & GR Harris Funeral Homes Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabranes, Jose A', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephens, Aimee', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-25T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6f2916d-48d2-5b42-bde3-fa22b5286070', 'word_count': 1676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6f2916d-48d2-5b42-bde3-fa22b5286070'}, {'abstract': 'When someone who is living paycheck to paycheck falls victim to an online fraud or a breach, the cascade of repercussions can be devastating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/25/opinion/privacy-poverty.html', 'snippet': 'When someone who is living paycheck to paycheck falls victim to an online fraud or a breach, the cascade of repercussions can be devastating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the tragic ironies of the digital age is this: Despite the fact that low-income Americans have experienced a long history of disproportionate surveillance, their unique privacy and security concerns are rarely visible in Washington and Silicon Valley. As my colleague Michele Gilman has noted, the poor often bear the burden of both ends of the spectrum of privacy harms; they are subjected to greater suspicion and monitoring when they apply for government benefits and live in heavily policed neighborhoods, but they can also lose out on education and job opportunities when their online profiles and employment histories aren’t visible (or curated) enough.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/03/opinion/sunday/25Madden/192291eef7d54ae0a95b2e96aaf74643-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/03/opinion/sunday/25Madden/192291eef7d54ae0a95b2e96aaf74643-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/03/opinion/sunday/25Madden/192291eef7d54ae0a95b2e96aaf74643-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/03/opinion/sunday/25Madden/192291eef7d54ae0a95b2e96aaf74643-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/03/opinion/sunday/25Madden/192291eef7d54ae0a95b2e96aaf74643-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/03/opinion/sunday/25Madden/192291eef7d54ae0a95b2e96aaf74643-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/03/opinion/sunday/25Madden/192291eef7d54ae0a95b2e96aaf74643-thu