ng', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Cities, Ranked by Age Group', 'kicker': 'Calculator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Best Cities for Your Age Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Millennial Generation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Generation X', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-25T13:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kolomatsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolomatsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4594008f-26f1-5ffd-91dd-508701e1f966', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4594008f-26f1-5ffd-91dd-508701e1f966'}, {'abstract': 'François Pinault, one of France’s richest men, is investing nearly $170 million in the Bourse de Commerce. Works from his own collection are set to go on display starting in 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/25/arts/design/bourse-de-commerce-paris-francois-pinault.html', 'snippet': 'François Pinault, one of France’s richest men, is investing nearly $170 million in the Bourse de Commerce. Works from his own collection are set to go on display starting in 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Early next year, after a nearly $170 million redevelopment, Paris’s 130-year-old Bourse de Commerce will reopen as a contemporary art museum. Unlike the world-famous state-funded museums nearby against which it hopes to measure up — namely, the Louvre and the Pompidou Center — this one will be financed by one man: the French billionaire François Pinault, whose collection consists of about 5,000 works by artists such as Jeff Koons, Cy Twombly, and Cindy Sherman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/25/arts/25bourse-oak1/merlin_153393540_ce1ba02b-217a-451f-afb6-3fcdc2827162-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/25/arts/25bourse-oak1/merlin_153393540_ce1ba02b-217a-451f-afb6-3fcdc2827162-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/25/arts/25bourse-oak1/merlin_153393540_ce1ba02b-217a-451f-afb6-3fcdc2827162-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/25/arts/25bourse-oak1/merlin_153393540_ce1ba02b-217a-451f-afb6-3fcdc2827162-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/25/arts/25bourse-oak1/25bourse-oak1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/25/arts/25bourse-oak1/25bourse-oak1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/25/arts/25bourse-oak1/25bourse-oak1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris I