ott captured the egomania and wanton development of New York’s streetscapes almost a century ago. The city is still at it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/25/lens/berenice-abbott-portraits-of-modernity-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Berenice Abbott captured the egomania and wanton development of New York’s streetscapes almost a century ago. The city is still at it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York skyline, wrote John Atlee Kouwenhoven in 1961, is not meant to make sense. “It is the product of insane politics, greed, competitive ostentation, megalomania, the worship of false gods. Its byproducts, in turn, are traffic jams, bad ventilation, noise, and all the other ills that metropolitan flesh is heir to. And the net result is, illogically enough, one of the most exaltedly beautiful things that mankind has ever made.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/lens/26Abbott1/26Abbott1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/26/lens/26Abbott1/26Abbott1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/lens/26Abbott1/26Abbott1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/lens/26Abbott1/26Abbott1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1583, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/lens/26Abbott1/26Abbott1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thu