y what growing up is like, and he’ll likely give answers that are starkly different from the endless displays of male determination and domination we often see in entertainment. Rather, the process of growing up can make even the most confident of boys feel lost, aimless, confused and powerless. Three new Y.A. novels explore that tension, showcasing different tenors of young male vulnerability.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/books/review/28franklin0/28franklin0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/books/review/28franklin0/28franklin0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/books/review/28franklin0/28franklin0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/books/review/28franklin0/28franklin0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1233, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/books/review/28franklin0/28franklin0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/28/books/review/28franklin0/28franklin0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/books/review/28franklin0/28franklin0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', '