', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/nyregion/26weinstein1/merlin_154007904_146d2099-20e4-448a-ab48-b3e23e97bd30-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/nyregion/26weinstein1/26weinstein1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/26/nyregion/26weinstein1/26weinstein1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/nyregion/26weinstein1/26weinstein1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Several Women May Testify Against Weinstein. But a Judge Is Keeping the List of Who Secret.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hearing on Weinstein Witnesses Will Be Private', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-26T16:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/175b7392-6069-584e-a4dd-e6f0bb167e45', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/175b7392-6069-584e-a4dd-e6f0bb167e45'}, {'abstract': 'A tour of SoHo galleries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/26/arts/design/gallery-guide-soho.html', 'snippet': 'A tour of SoHo galleries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been decades since the great powers of the New York City art world decamped for Chelsea, but SoHo remains dotted with galleries of long standing like Ronald Feldman; numerous newer arrivals; small museums like the Drawing Center, the Donald Judd Foundation and the Center for Italian Modern Art; and the magisterial Dia Art Foundation, with its permanent installations of Walter De Maria’s “Earth Room” and “The Broken Kilometer.” Here are five of the most notable gallery shows up right now or opening soon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Fagerskiold/merlin_153572295_5a8fe29f-7c8c-4103-b6d1-17cc9c144bf2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Fagerskiold/merlin_153572295_5a8fe29f-7c8c-4103-b6d1-17cc9c144bf2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Fagerskiold/merlin_153572295_5a8fe29f-7c8c-4103-b6d1-17cc9c144bf2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Fagerskiold/merlin_153572295_5a8fe29f-7c8c-4103-b6d1-17cc9c144bf2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Fagerskiold/25springgallery-Fagerskiold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Fagerskiold/25springgallery-Fagerskiold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Fagerskiold/25springgallery-Fagerskiold-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Gallery Guide: SoHo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-26T16:22:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Heinrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heinrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0f705cc-e575-5c5f-b837-cdeb9a85bd00', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0f705cc-e575-5c5f-b837-cdeb9a85bd00'}, {'abstract': 'A tour of Chelsea galleries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/26/arts/design/gallery-guide-chelsea.html', 'snippet': 'A tour of Chelsea galleries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art and real estate development met elsewhere in the city, but they got married in Chelsea. Tall, expensive buildings are rising around 10th Avenue, and gallery rents are rising along with them. Young art dealers arrive to try their hand in the official gallery neighborhood, and often fold-up shop quickly, as the promisingly offbeat American Medium, which started in Brooklyn, did recently. The juggernaut of mega-gallery showrooms continues, with behemoths like Hauser & Wirth mounting impressive historical shows (and starting their own bookstores, publishing houses, magazines and nonprofit foundations), and David Zwirner is planning a Renzo Piano-designed space to open in 2020. Meanwhile, the High Line looms ubiquitously overhead, like a people mover transporting tourists (mostly) from the new Hudson Yards on the north end to the gleaming Whitney Museum of American Art on the south. Contemporary art is everywhere though, including the High Line, where you’ll find a monumental sculpture by Simone Leigh, who just opened a show at the Guggenheim, along with other notable displays. Art has saturated the neighborhood, and you can see everything from work by emerging artists to the long deceased. Here are a few places to start. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-smith/25springgallery-smith-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-smith/25springgallery-smith-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-smith/25springgallery-smith-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-smith/25springgallery-smith-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-smith/25springgallery-smith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-smith/25springgallery-smith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-smith/25springgallery-smith-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Gallery Guide: Chelsea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-26T16:24:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c0505f-d1ce-562b-b901-bfca2c93f5de', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c0505f-d1ce-562b-b901-bfca2c93f5de'}, {'abstract': 'A tour of Upper East Side galleries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/26/arts/design/gallery-guide-upper-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'A tour of Upper East Side galleries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cockamamie real estate market has turned the good old Upper East Side into the most stimulating gallery neighborhood in New York — and as downtown stultifies and Chelsea wilts in the shadow of Hudson Yards, the old blue-blood quarter has grown manifold. Up here the big-ticket dealers in grand townhouses exhibit alongside younger galleries in walk-ups and outposts of international dealers; the last few years have welcomed Nara Roesler and Mendes Wood of São Paulo, Almine Rech of Paris, Simon Lee of London and Kurimanzutto of Mexico City. That’s not to mention the dealers in antiquities, Asian art and rare books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Iturbide/merlin_153735726_2c7da623-754b-4933-8ef5-d2ef67893ae1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Iturbide/merlin_153735726_2c7da623-754b-4933-8ef5-d2ef67893ae1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 684}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Iturbide/merlin_153735726_2c7da623-754b-4933-8ef5-d2ef67893ae1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Iturbide/merlin_153735726_2c7da623-754b-4933-8ef5-d2ef67893ae1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1797, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Iturbide/25springgallery-Iturbide-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Iturbide/25springgallery-Iturbide-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-Iturbide/25springgallery-Iturbide-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Gallery Guide: Upper East Side', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-26T16:26:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Farago', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farago', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b831b42-49f5-5080-b691-5b72dc2a87d6', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b831b42-49f5-5080-b691-5b72dc2a87d6'}, {'abstract': 'A tour of Lower East Side galleries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/26/arts/design/gallery-guide-lower-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'A tour of Lower East Side galleries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The arc of the Lower East Side gallery scene bends toward youth. It is probably home to the greatest number of starting-out dealers showing the works of emerging artists in New York. This gives the art scene in this neighborhood and the ones developing around it — in NoHo, East Village South, Chinatown or Little Italy — a certain lightness of being. We’re often looking at first, not necessarily mature or final, artistic statements. It helps that the area lacks the dwarfing juggernaut of big-name, property-proud galleries and blue-chip artists that give Chelsea or the Upper East Side their weight. Most of the shows reviewed here emphasize youth in various forms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-niles/merlin_153653493_753def72-05d6-4f55-aead-8319360769ab-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-niles/merlin_153653493_753def72-05d6-4f55-aead-8319360769ab-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 874}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-niles/merlin_153653493_753def72-05d6-4f55-aead-8319360769ab-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 704, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-niles/merlin_153653493_753def72-05d6-4f55-aead-8319360769ab-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1407, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-niles/25springgallery-niles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-niles/25springgallery-niles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-niles/25springgallery-niles-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Gallery Guide: Lower East Side', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chapter NY (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lyles & King (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pierogi 2000', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uffner, Rachel, Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Simone Subal (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niles, Arcmanoro', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-26T16:28:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15594a14-a1ed-525d-a6de-a7cc6633bfbd', 'word_count': 1278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15594a14-a1ed-525d-a6de-a7cc6633bfbd'}, {'abstract': 'A tour of Canal Street galleries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/26/arts/design/gallery-guide-canal-street.html', 'snippet': 'A tour of Canal Street galleries.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The art world should be understood as a complex ecology with many microclimates and some macro ones,” said the curator Okwui Enwezor, who died in March. He could have been describing the geography of New York City galleries. In the 1970s, the climates were macro and few (the Upper East Side, SoHo). In the 1980s, they were joined by the East Village; in the 1990s, by Chelsea; and in the 2000s, by the Lower East Side and Brooklyn. And there are spillovers everywhere. Today, it can be hard to tag a gallery by district, as I learned when visiting a handful that straddle either side of Canal Street, a cross-island axis that runs from SoHo to Chinatown, without claiming full allegiance to either. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-brown/25springgallery-brown-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-brown/25springgallery-brown-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 748}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-brown/25springgallery-brown-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 822, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-brown/25springgallery-brown-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 1116, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-brown/25springgallery-brown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-brown/25springgallery-brown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/26/arts/26springgallery-brown/25springgallery-brown-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'