Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-27T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maureen Dowd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maureen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/975f5d0e-2ca9-5f68-aa51-550440ceac71', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/975f5d0e-2ca9-5f68-aa51-550440ceac71'}, {'abstract': 'Only in America is the word freighted with so much perceived menace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/27/opinion/sunday/socialism.html', 'snippet': 'Only in America is the word freighted with so much perceived menace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To be trapped in the boarding area of a smallish airport in the upper Midwest is, as often as not, to be subjected to that bestial din of fricatives, gutturals, plosives and shrieks of hysterical alarm that constitutes political discussion on Fox News, pouring incessantly from those obnoxious pendulous ceiling televisions. And unless one fancies running the T.S.A.’s gantlet of gropers again, there’s no escape. The experience is especially nasty if one’s wait coincides with the prime-time shows hosted by those two almost indistinguishable fellows with the suety faces, bouffant coiffures and nerve-racking mezzo-castrato voices.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28hart/merlin_153327828_4204424d-b476-4ce0-b17f-5171181d63ae-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28hart/merlin_153327828_4204424d-b476-4ce0-b17f-5171181d63ae-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28hart/merlin_153327828_4204424d-b476-4ce0-b17f-5171181d63ae-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28hart/merlin_153327828_4204424d-b476-4ce0-b17f-5171181d63ae-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28hart/merlin_153327828_4204424d-b476-4ce0-b17f-5171181d63ae-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28hart/merlin_153327828_4204424d-b476-4ce0-b17f-5171181d63ae-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28hart/merlin_153327828_4204424d-b476-4ce0-b17f-5171181d63ae-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can We Please Relax About ‘Socialism’?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Socialism’ Is Not a Scary Word', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socialism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocasio-Cortez, Alexandria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-27T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bentley Hart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'Bentley', 'lastname': 'Hart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8d92166-e687-5143-86ab-750a9544ea46', 'word_count': 1290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8d92166-e687-5143-86ab-750a9544ea46'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve long been obsessed with shadowy puppet masters. Then I found one in an Israeli retirement home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/27/opinion/sunday/my-grandma-rasputin.html', 'snippet': 'I’ve long been obsessed with shadowy puppet masters. Then I found one in an Israeli retirement home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few months ago, I was in the back seat of a cab in New York with my parents. They were having the kind of conversation that’s easy to ignore: flight plans, work grievances, my father’s mother’s recent move to a nursing home at a small town in central Israel. I zoned out. Then I heard them grumbling. Something about how my grandma, Talia, had been sowing trouble at the nursing home. Something about how she had quietly, behind the scenes, fomented an insurrection. I turned to look at my parents with a squint and they smiled. Because they realized that they had been, unintentionally, describing just the kind of character that I’ve been obsessing over for years.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/28barshad/merlin_154011438_2e4c0104-0449-4df3-9f38-5125232e4ba9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/28barshad/merlin_154011438_2e4c0104-0449-4df3-9f38-5125232e4ba9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 983}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/28barshad/merlin_154011438_2e4c0104-0449-4df3-9f38-5125232e4ba9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/28barshad/merlin_154011438_2e4c0104-0449-4df3-9f38-5125232e4ba9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1250, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/28barshad/28barshad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/28barshad/28barshad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/28barshad/28barshad-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Grandma, Rasputin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Grandma, Rasputin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-27T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amos Barshad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barshad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec2758ec-18df-567a-85c1-6289ebfe8042', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec2758ec-18df-567a-85c1-6289ebfe8042'}, {'abstract': 'Let us reassure you: You’re worried only because you don’t understand anything about anything.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/27/opinion/sunday/your-privacy-is-our-business.html', 'snippet': 'Let us reassure you: You’re worried only because you don’t understand anything about anything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You look upset. You’ve been making a lot of noise lately about deleting our company’s app from your phone. But please, sit down. Let me explain. You just don’t understand how technology works.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28loose/28loose-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 557, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28loose/28loose-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 557}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28loose/28loose-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 951, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28loose/28loose-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1902, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption'