th care and compassion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My patient, an octogenarian with pneumonia and acute leukemia, was too frail to tolerate the standard treatment for his cancer, and trying to cure his pneumonia with intravenous antibiotics, when the leukemia had already compromised his immune system, would only have weakened him further. It made sense to switch him to “comfort measures”: to focus on alleviating his suffering rather than curing him. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28brown/b27e7ab39e2048baa40450697f68c92c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28brown/b27e7ab39e2048baa40450697f68c92c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 476}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28brown/b27e7ab39e2048baa40450697f68c92c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28brown/b27e7ab39e2048baa40450697f68c92c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1625, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28brown/28brown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28brown/28brown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28brown/28brown-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make Doctors Think About Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Doctors Think About Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospice Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-27T18:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Theresa Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba93eda6-1513-560f-9471-248e137d1e67', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba93eda6-1513-560f-9471-248e137d1e67'}, {'abstract': 'The American family needs defending and right now men are leading the charge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/27/opinion/sunday/conservative-women.html', 'snippet': 'The American family needs defending and right now men are leading the charge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty years ago, Phyllis Schlafly hosted a gala for 1,100 guests at the Shoreham Hotel in Washington to celebrate the expiration of the deadline to ratify the Equal Rights Amendment. A bomb threat was not enough to dampen the evening’s festivities, which included not only dinner and speeches but a musical revue featuring parodies of “The Impossible Dream” and “Old-Fashioned Girl” with lyrics adapted for the occasion by Schlafly herself. The celebration did not just mark the end of the E.R.A., Schlafly later said, but “the end of an era, the era of conservative defeats.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28andrews1/28andrews1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28andrews1/28andrews1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 682}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28andrews1/28andrews1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28andrews1/28andrews1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1803, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28andrews1/28andrews1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28andrews1/28andrews1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/28/opinion/sunday/28andrews1/28andrews1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Are the Socially Conservative Women in This Fight?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Will Defend the American Family?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schlafly, Phyllis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-27T18:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helen Andrews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andrews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/011d0221-2c7e-568c-a560-8a8bb540710d', 'word_count': 2822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/011d0221-2c7e-568c-a560-8a8bb540710d'}, {'abstract': 'Children of privilege, like Abigail Disney, are taking a moral stand against inequality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/27/opinion/sunday/rich-social-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'Children of privilege, like Abigail Disney, are taking a moral stand against inequality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This country is rigged in favor of making the very wealthy even wealthier. That’s what Democrats keep saying on the 2020 campaign trail. And it’s what some of the people who have reaped the rewards of this rigged system think too. Abigail Disney, granddaughter of Roy Disney, is one recent high-profile example. On Tuesday, she called out the “naked indecency” of the $65 million in compensation that goes to Disney’s chief executive, Bob Iger. That figure, she noted, is “1,424 times the median pay of a Disney worker.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/sunday/28sherman1/28sherman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/sunday/28sherman1/28sherman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/sunday/28sherman1/28sherman1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/sunday/28sherman1/28sherman1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/sunday/28sherman1/28sherman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/sunday/28sherman1/28sherman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/opinion/sunday/28sherman1/28sherman1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rich Kid Revolutionaries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Rich Kid Revolutionaries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequalit