limate change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When John Barrasso, a Republican from oil and uranium-rich Wyoming who has spent years blocking climate change legislation, introduced a bill this year to promote nuclear energy, he added a twist: a desire to tackle global warming.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/science/00cli-republicans-1-promo/00cli-republicans-1-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/04/29/science/00cli-republicans-1-promo/00cli-republicans-1-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/science/00cli-republicans-1-promo/00cli-republicans-1-promo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/science/00cli-republicans-1-promo/00cli-republicans-1-promo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1660, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/science/00cli-republicans-1-promo/00cli-republicans-1-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/04/29/science/00cli-republicans-1-promo/00cli-republicans-1-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/04/29/science/00cli-republicans-1-promo/00cli-republicans-1-promo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Switch, Some Republicans Start Citing Climate Change as Driving Their Policies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Shift for Republicans, Some Point to Climate When Proposing Policy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Green New Deal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrasso, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-30T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96b780ab-a4f8-5d17-a82f-db7b33f0246e', 'word_count': 1432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96b780ab-a4f8-5d17-a82f-db7b33f0246e'}, {'abstract': 'Minimalist cabins, flower-dusted salads, a floating sauna: Even the fat flies and creeping spiders can’t undermine the magic of this hidden retreat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/30/travel/swedish-woods-retreat-camp.html', 'snippet': 'Minimalist cabins, flower-dusted salads, a floating sauna: Even the fat flies and creeping spiders can’t undermine the magic of this hidden retreat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story of Stedsans in the Woods, as told on Instagram, reads like a modern-day fairy tale: a rural retreat deep in the forest of southern Sweden where the sun is always setting over a lake, campfire gatherings glow nightly, and every meal is a nourishing Nordic feast of food foraged and farm-raised. The wholesome appeal of this remote utopia among pines and old-growth oaks beckons through even the smallest of digital screens. But is social media enough to convince anyone to drive hours for a night in the woods?', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/travel/03Sweden-Woods6/merlin_144370455_34e625b6-e75e-4085-af55-c6cf7d118f62-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/05/travel/03Sweden-Woods6/merlin_144370455_34e625b6-e75e-4085-af55-c6cf7d118f62-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/travel/03Sweden-Woods6/merlin_144370455_34e625b6-e75e-4085-af55-c6cf7d118f62-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/travel/03Sweden-Woods6/merlin_144370455_34e625b6-e75e-4085-af55-c6cf7d118f62-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/05/travel/03Sweden-Woods6/03Sweden-Woods6-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/05/travel/03Sweden-Woods6/03Sweden-Woods6-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarg