lue': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Demme, Jonathan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singleton, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Spike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Boyz n the Hood (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Poetic Justice (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-04-30T13:40:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Fretts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fretts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd572d7b-18f1-57b9-bce0-7099b33430ac', 'word_count': 1310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd572d7b-18f1-57b9-bce0-7099b33430ac'}, {'abstract': 'His influence extended backward and forward; a look at some of the ways he changed the course of American movies, like the work of Barry Jenkins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/30/movies/john-singleton-boyz-n-the-hood.html', 'snippet': 'His influence extended backward and forward; a look at some of the ways he changed the course of American movies, like the work of Barry Jenkins.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Boyz N the Hood” rests in American movie history like a boulder in a riverbed, altering the direction of the stream. After its release in the summer of 1991, everything looked different, including its precursors. “Mean Streets,” “Rebel Without a Cause,” the Blaxploitation spectacles of the 1970s, the socially conscious crime dramas of the 1930s, classic westerns and samurai epics — somehow John Singleton, a very recent graduate of the University of Southern California film school, synthesized all of those models even as he came up with something bracingly, thrillingly and frighteningly new.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/arts/30singleton-appraisal2/30singleton-appraisal2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/05/01/arts/30singleton-appraisal2/30singleton-appraisal2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/arts/30singleton-appraisal2/30singleton-appraisal2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/arts/30singleton-appraisal2/30singleton-appraisal2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/arts/30singleton-appraisal2/30singleton-appraisal2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/05/01/arts/30singleton-appraisal2/30singleton-appraisal2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/05/01/arts/30singleton-appraisal2/30singleton-appraisal2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Singleton Did Justice to a Poetic Vision of African-American Life', 'kicker': 'An Appraisal',